(Neural Networks and Backpropagation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A feed-forward network stacks linear layers with nonlinear) Tj
T*
(activation functions such as ReLU. Without the nonlinearity the) Tj
T*
(stack would collapse to a single linear map. Backpropagation) Tj
T*
(computes gradients layer by layer using the chain rule, reusing) Tj
T*
(intermediate results from the forward pass.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Training tricks from the lectures: use mini-batches rather than the) Tj
T*
(full data set, apply dropout to reduce overfitting, and normalize) Tj
T*
(the inputs. Weight initialization matters: Xavier initialization for) Tj
T*
(tanh networks, He initialization for ReLU networks.) Tj
T*
